BT 1 0 0 1 0 243.804 Tm .2355 Tw 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: Yes. The undertaking is a valid subject of insurance because both parties were ignorant of the) Tj T* 0 Tw (loss when the contract was perfected.) Tj  T* 2.571692 Tw (Under Section 2\(a\) of the Insurance Code, insurance is an undertaking for consideration to) Tj T* 0 Tw .528 Tw (indemnify against loss from an unknown or contingent event, and under Section 3, insurance on) Tj T* 0 Tw .082588 Tw (a past event is allowed when the parties do not know whether it has already happened. Fortuity is) Tj T* 0 Tw (therefore judged at perfection, and ignorance shared by both sides preserves it.) Tj  T* .116 Tw (Here, each element is present on these facts. The P10,000 is the consideration. The P1,000,000 is) Tj T* 0 Tw .0256 Tw (the promised indemnity. The arrival or nonarrival of the named ship is the contingent event. Both) Tj T* 0 Tw .711529 Tw (X and Y were ignorant of the loss at perfection, so the counter-reading that an already lost ship) Tj T* 0 Tw (cannot be insured fails under the Section 3 unknown-past rule.) Tj  T* 1.752923 Tw (The subject is therefore insurable. The contract is enforceable once insurable interest and the) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.210154 Tw (remaining requisites are shown, and the loss is payable within the agreed indemnity. Insurable) Tj T* 0 Tw .808941 Tw (interest remains the gatekeeper, as in La O v. Yek Tong Lin Fire and Marine \(G.R. No. 33131,) Tj T* 0 Tw (1930\), where recovery turned on identifying the holder of the damnifiable interest.) Tj T* ET
