BT 1 0 0 1 0 225.804 Tm 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: Recovery is scaled down to P900,000. The insured does not get the full P1,500,000.) Tj  T* 4.078286 Tw (Under Section 17 of the Insurance Code, the measure of property interest is capped at) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.394 Tw (damnification, applied through the ratable-proportion rule, under which the insured is his own) Tj T* 0 Tw .672857 Tw (insurer for the uninsured excess \(Galian v. State Assurance Co., G.R. No. L-8405, February 10,) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.814571 Tw (1915\). Partial loss therefore equals actual loss multiplied by insured value over value at fire.) Tj T* 0 Tw (Coinsurance punishes underinsurance rather than rewarding it.) Tj  T* .0704 Tw (Here, the figures trigger the scale-down. The building is worth P5,000,000 but is insured for only) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.431714 Tw (P3,000,000, so the insured carried two-fifths of the risk. The P1,500,000 partial fire loss is) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.337091 Tw (multiplied by three-fifths, yielding P900,000. The counter-reading that any loss below the) Tj T* 0 Tw .2952 Tw (P3,000,000 face amount is paid in full fails because the 60 percent coinsurance clause makes the) Tj T* 0 Tw (insured coinsure the uncovered portion.) Tj  T* .0944 Tw (The insurer therefore pays only P900,000, and the insured bears the P600,000 balance as his own) Tj T* 0 Tw (insurer.) Tj T* ET
