BT 1 0 0 1 0 225.804 Tm .630353 Tw 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: The endorsement forms no part of the contract, so the Building A claim stands on the policy) Tj T* 0 Tw (as written.) Tj  T* 5.031692 Tw (Under Section 50 of the Insurance Code, the policy must carry the seven mandatory) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.003385 Tw (specifications, applied with Article 1377 of the Civil Code, under which obscurity is construed) Tj T* 0 Tw .577714 Tw (against the drafter, and with the adhesion rule, under which ambiguities are resolved against the) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.984 Tw (insurer to avoid forfeiture \(Qua Chee Gan v. Law Union and Rock Insurance Co., G.R. No.) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.173714 Tw (L-4611, December 17, 1955\). Riders become part of the contract only when attached to the) Tj T* 0 Tw (policy, referred to in it, and supported by premium.) Tj  T* .2288 Tw (Here, the endorsement fails every test. It is unsigned, unattached, and unreferred to in the policy.) Tj T* 0 Tw .8272 Tw (The counter-reading that the insurer may invoke an unattached paper to deny a Building B loss) Tj T* 0 Tw (fails because an unmentioned endorsement binds no one.) Tj  T* .4496 Tw (The endorsement is therefore disregarded entirely, and the Building A fire loss is payable in full) Tj T* 0 Tw (within the written terms and limits of the policy.) Tj T* ET
