BT 1 0 0 1 0 279.804 Tm 1.518462 Tw 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: No. Rescission will not prosper. The undisclosed port congestion surcharge practice was a) Tj T* 0 Tw .164471 Tw (general usage of trade equally open to the insurer, so there was no concealment of a material fact) Tj T* 0 Tw (the insurer had no means of ascertaining.) Tj  T* 1.3168 Tw (Under Sec. 28 of the Insurance Code, each party must communicate in good faith all material) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.1616 Tw (facts within his knowledge which the other has no means of ascertaining. Under Sec. 32, each) Tj T* 0 Tw .690353 Tw (party is bound to know all general causes open to inquiry equally with the other and all general) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.27575 Tw (usages of trade. Under Sec. 33, the right to material information may be waived by neglect to) Tj T* 0 Tw (inquire where the fact is distinctly implied in communicated facts.) Tj  T* 1.669714 Tw (Here P disclosed the voyage route, which distinctly implied exposure to port costs, while the) Tj T* 0 Tw .270857 Tw (surcharge practice was well known in the trade and equally accessible to the marine underwriter.) Tj T* 0 Tw .411429 Tw (The insurer asked no question on surcharges and issued the policy. The counter-reading that any) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.65 Tw (undisclosed cost practice is concealment fails because Secs. 28 and 32 excuse what the other) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.9856 Tw (could ascertain and charge the insurer with usages of trade, and Sec. 33 treats the neglected) Tj T* 0 Tw (inquiry as waiver.) Tj  T* .27675 Tw (There is therefore no concealment under Secs. 26 to 27. The policy stands, the insurer is deemed) Tj T* 0 Tw (to have waived the information, and the rescission action must be dismissed.) Tj T* ET
