BT 1 0 0 1 0 225.804 Tm 1.105846 Tw 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (misrepresentation, as Manila Bankers Life v. Aban \(G.R. No. 175666, 2013\) holds that styling) Tj T* 0 Tw (the defense as nullity does not evade the bar.) Tj ( ) Tj T* .031714 Tw (Here Diego delivered his application and premium to Gabriela, the officer in charge of approving) Tj T* 0 Tw .2355 Tw (life policies, and Gabriela knew of the cancer yet approved the application on June 1, 2020. That) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.826571 Tw (knowledge is GIC's knowledge, so GIC had the means of ascertaining the illness and cannot) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.525818 Tw (plead concealment. The counter-reading that Gabriela concealed the illness from her own) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.7072 Tw (company fails because the officer's breach of duty to her principal is not concealment by the) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.4168 Tw (applicant, and the insurer's remedy was against its officer and not the heirs. Diego died on) Tj T* 0 Tw .1515 Tw (January 30, 2023 in a vehicular accident, about two years and eight months after approval, so the) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.0064 Tw (two-year bar had long run and the accidental death confirms materiality is never judged by the) Tj T* 0 Tw (event.) Tj ( ) Tj T* 1.364571 Tw (GIC therefore holds no concealment defense and no timely fraud defense. The denial must be) Tj T* 0 Tw (reversed, the proceeds must be paid to the heirs, and GIC's recourse, if any, lies against Gabriela.) Tj T* ET
