BT 1 0 0 1 0 315.804 Tm .260471 Tw 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: Yes. The insurer may rescind if the concrete-wall statement is false in a material point, and A) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.293429 Tw (may not invoke the caretaker remark or use the representation to contradict the express policy) Tj T* 0 Tw (term.) Tj  T* 2.143059 Tw (Under Secs. 44 to 46 of the Insurance Code, a representation is false when the facts fail to) Tj T* 0 Tw .124286 Tw (correspond with its assertions, and if false in a material point, whether affirmative or promissory,) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.339385 Tw (the injured party may rescind from the time the representation becomes false, with materiality) Tj T* 0 Tw .554571 Tw (tested as in concealment. Under Sec. 40, a representation cannot qualify an express provision of) Tj T* 0 Tw (the policy, though it may qualify an implied warranty.) Tj  T* 1.300941 Tw (Here A stated the warehouse was concrete walled when it was half timber, so the facts fail to) Tj T* 0 Tw .775385 Tw (correspond with the assertion and the representation is false. Wall construction plainly bears on) Tj T* 0 Tw .4944 Tw (fire underwriting, so the falsity is material. The counter-readings fail one by one. The claim that) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.4064 Tw (the caretaker sourcing excuses the falsity fails because A adopted the statement as his own to) Tj T* 0 Tw .079333 Tw (obtain cover, and one who asserts as fact what he has not verified assumes the risk of falsity. The) Tj T* 0 Tw .4048 Tw (attempt to soften the expressly issued term fails because Sec. 40 gives the express description of) Tj T* 0 Tw (concrete throughout priority over the collateral remark.) Tj  T* 1.245429 Tw (The insurer is therefore entitled to rescind from the time the representation became false upon) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.959714 Tw (proving materiality at trial. The policy cannot be read down by the caretaker remark, and) Tj T* 0 Tw (indemnity need not be paid under the avoided contract.) Tj T* ET
