BT 1 0 0 1 0 333.804 Tm .7125 Tw 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: No. The insurer may not avoid the policy on the hydrant warranty alone. Its prior inspection) Tj T* 0 Tw .927692 Tw (with knowledge, followed by two years of premium collection, estops the defense, and without) Tj T* 0 Tw (fraud Sec. 76 gives only exoneration while breached rather than avoidance.) Tj  T* 1.13025 Tw (Under Secs. 74 to 76 of the Insurance Code, violation of a material warranty entitles the other) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.4032 Tw (party to rescind, but breach of an immaterial provision does not avoid the policy unless so) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.266154 Tw (declared, and breach of warranty without fraud merely exonerates the insurer from the time) Tj T* 0 Tw .00675 Tw (breach occurs or prevents attachment if broken in inception. As Qua Chee Gan v. Law Union and) Tj T* 0 Tw .100286 Tw (Rock Insurance \(G.R. No. L-4611, 1955\) holds, an insurer that inspects, knows the premises lack) Tj T* 0 Tw .826154 Tw (the warranted appliances, yet issues the policy and keeps collecting premiums is estopped from) Tj T* 0 Tw (invoking the warranties, with ambiguities construed against it.) Tj  T* .153333 Tw (Here the warranty called for two 2.5-inch hydrants at 100 psi at all times, yet the insurer saw one) Tj T* 0 Tw 4.98 Tw (weak hydrant at issuance, issued anyway, and collected premiums for two years. The) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.269429 Tw (counter-reading that any paper breach voids the policy fails twice. It fails on estoppel because) Tj T* 0 Tw .0048 Tw (knowing issuance plus continued collection is waiver by conduct under Qua Chee Gan. It fails on) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.196 Tw (remedy because with no fraud shown, Sec. 76 does not convert a supervening shortfall into) Tj T* 0 Tw (voidness from the beginning.) Tj  T* .7848 Tw (The warranty defense therefore fails. The insurer remains liable on the fire loss, subject only to) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.4264 Tw (proving some other valid defense, and it cannot treat the whole policy as void from the) Tj T* 0 Tw (beginning.) Tj T* ET
