BT 1 0 0 1 0 279.804 Tm .672 Tw 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: Contention 2 fails. The January 2019 suicide, about three years after the January 2016 issue,) Tj T* 0 Tw (falls outside the suicide exclusion, so XYZ remains liable on this ground.) Tj  T* 3.25575 Tw (Under Sec. 183 of the Insurance Code, the insurer in a life contract is liable for suicide) Tj T* 0 Tw .56775 Tw (committed after the policy has been in force for two years from issue or last reinstatement, with) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.842 Tw (insanity suicide always compensable and shorter policy periods measured accordingly. Under) Tj T* 0 Tw .8056 Tw (Secs. 86 to 89, exclusions are strictly construed against the insurer, which carries the burden of) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.252615 Tw (proving the exception after the beneficiary's prima facie case, as United Merchants v. Country) Tj T* 0 Tw (Bankers \(G.R. No. 198588, 2012\) holds on the burden sequence.) Tj  T* .09 Tw (Here the policy ran from January 2016 to January 2019, about three years of continuous force, so) Tj T* 0 Tw .408857 Tw (the two-year suicide threshold is passed. XYZ proved no insanity question and no shorter policy) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.057846 Tw (period, and its blanket invocation of suicide cites no clause language. The counter-reading that) Tj T* 0 Tw .444 Tw (suicide is never compensable in life insurance fails because Sec. 183 draws the line at two years) Tj T* 0 Tw .031714 Tw (precisely to cover this case, and an unproved exclusion construed against the insurer cannot carry) Tj T* 0 Tw (the defense.) Tj  T* .159529 Tw (Contention 2 is therefore denied. XYZ is liable on the suicide ground, subject only to the Sec. 48) Tj T* 0 Tw (incontestability analysis that independently defeats contention 1.) Tj T* ET
