BT 1 0 0 1 0 297.804 Tm .065647 Tw 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: The forty-day delay in fire notice exonerates the insurer under Sec. 90 unless a Sec. 93 waiver) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.452 Tw (is proved, while the late-specified proof defect is waived under Sec. 92 and cannot defeat the) Tj T* 0 Tw (claim.) Tj  T* .88125 Tw (Under Sec. 90 of the Insurance Code, a fire insurer is exonerated unless written notice is given) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.6944 Tw (by the insured or a person entitled to the benefit of the insurance without unnecessary delay,) Tj T* 0 Tw .52725 Tw (while under Sec. 92 a remediable defect in notice or proof is waived unless the insurer specifies) Tj T* 0 Tw .963 Tw (it without unnecessary delay as a ground of objection, and under Sec. 93 delay itself is waived) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.6496 Tw (only where the insurer caused it or failed to object promptly and specifically on the delay) Tj T* 0 Tw (ground.) Tj  T* .8056 Tw (Here, the policy required written notice within fifteen days and the insured gave notice only on) Tj T* 0 Tw 5.7732 Tw (day forty without justification, which exceeds without unnecessary delay and triggers) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.458857 Tw (exoneration. The counter-reading that the cured proof saves the claim fails on the notice limb) Tj T* 0 Tw .052 Tw (because notice and proof are separate requisites, although it succeeds on the defect limb since the) Tj T* 0 Tw (insurer specified the proof defect late and therefore waived it.) Tj  T* .216 Tw (The insurer is therefore exonerated for the late notice unless the insured proves a Sec. 93 waiver,) Tj T* 0 Tw .58 Tw (but it can no longer rely on the waived proof defect, so the notice delay bars recovery while the) Tj T* 0 Tw (defect does not.) Tj T* ET
