BT 1 0 0 1 0 261.804 Tm .58575 Tw 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: The deduction is improper and the health insurer must pay the policy benefits in full without) Tj T* 0 Tw (subtracting the sick-leave pay.) Tj  T* 1.176857 Tw (Under the collateral source rule of the chapter, benefits received from a source independent of) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.2545 Tw (the insurer and the wrongdoer do not reduce the liability of the insurer on its own contract) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.055143 Tw (promise, and no double recovery results because total recovery stays capped at the loss. Under) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.148571 Tw (Secs. 95 and 96 of the Insurance Code, deduction and ratable contribution apply only between) Tj T* 0 Tw (co-insurers of the same person covering the same subject and the same interest.) Tj  T* .930462 Tw (Here, the sick-leave benefits come from the employer under the employment relation while the) Tj T* 0 Tw .470769 Tw (health benefits answer the separate insurance contract, so the employer is an independent source) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.007692 Tw (and not a co-insurer of the same interest. The counter-reading that any overlapping payment) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.418462 Tw (reduces the policy fails because the two benefits answer different promises, and the insurer) Tj T* 0 Tw (cannot borrow Secs. 95 and 96 for a same-person co-insurance adjustment that does not exist.) Tj  T* 1.3184 Tw (The insurer must therefore pay the health policy in full with aggregate recovery capped at the) Tj T* 0 Tw .504857 Tw (confinement loss, and any recourse runs through subrogation against the party liable for the loss) Tj T* 0 Tw (rather than by deduction from the insured.) Tj T* ET
