BT 1 0 0 1 0 315.804 Tm .7816 Tw 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: The insurer is liable for the proceeds plus double-ceiling interest running from May 31 until) Tj T* 0 Tw (full satisfaction, together with attorney's fees and proven expenses.) Tj  T* .08925 Tw (Under Sec. 249 of the Insurance Code, a non-life insurer must pay within thirty days after receipt) Tj T* 0 Tw .7608 Tw (of proof of loss plus ascertainment by agreement or arbitration, or within ninety days of receipt) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.885714 Tw (where no ascertainment is made within sixty days, with delay interest at twice the Monetary) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.312286 Tw (Board ceiling unless the claim is fraudulent. Under Sec. 250, missing the statutory deadline is) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.262154 Tw (prima facie unreasonable delay once the Commissioner or the court makes the finding in) Tj T* 0 Tw 4.721455 Tw (enforcement litigation, and the award carries attorney's fees and expenses plus running) Tj T* 0 Tw (double-ceiling interest.) Tj  T* 1.842 Tw (Here, complete proof of loss was received on March 1 and neither agreement nor arbitration) Tj T* 0 Tw .9825 Tw (fixed the amount within sixty days, so the ninety-day default fixed the deadline at May 30 and) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.030286 Tw (payment on day 120 came thirty days late. The counter-reading that heavy volume excuses the) Tj T* 0 Tw .044471 Tw (lapse fails because volume is not just cause, and no fraud defense was pleaded that could stop the) Tj T* 0 Tw .672 Tw (clocks under the rule in United Merchants Corp. v. Country Bankers Insurance Corp. \(G.R. No.) Tj T* 0 Tw (198588, 2012\).) Tj  T* .904615 Tw (The insured therefore recovers the proceeds with double-ceiling interest from May 31 until full) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.689 Tw (satisfaction plus attorney's fees and proven expenses, with the delay deemed prima facie) Tj T* 0 Tw (unreasonable under Sec. 250.) Tj T* ET
