BT 1 0 0 1 0 279.804 Tm .9856 Tw 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: The hospital perks are neither pre-need plans under Sec. 4\(b\) nor HMO contracts under EO) Tj T* 0 Tw (192 s. 2015, so they fall outside pre-need regulation and stand as mere shareholder incentives.) Tj  T* 3.00675 Tw (Under Sec. 4\(b\) of RA 9829, a pre-need plan is a contract for the benefit of planholders) Tj T* 0 Tw .4744 Tw (providing future service or money or other benefit at actual need or agreed maturity as specified) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.71225 Tw (therein in exchange for cash or installment amounts. Under EO 192 s. 2015 as applied in IC) Tj T* 0 Tw .272571 Tw (Letter Opinion 2022-01, an HMO contract delivers pre-agreed health care for a fixed prepaid fee) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.1832 Tw (over a period through a provider network. Under Gaw v. CA \(G.R. No. 147748, 2006\), the) Tj T* 0 Tw (written plan terms control the classification because the plan is the law between the parties.) Tj  T* .052 Tw (Here, the free and discounted board and procedures and drugs go to subscribers and their spouses) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.827692 Tw (and dependents as incentives for stock subscription rather than as specified benefits at actual) Tj T* 0 Tw .930462 Tw (need or agreed maturity paid for with plan consideration. The arrangement likewise collects no) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.031429 Tw (fixed prepaid membership fee over a period and operates no provider network, so the HMO) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.210769 Tw (definition fails on both price and structure. Treating share incentives as plan benefits would) Tj T* 0 Tw (rewrite the Sec. 4\(b\) exchange element that Gaw enforces literally.) Tj  T* 1.272857 Tw (The perks are therefore neither pre-need plans nor HMO contracts, and no pre-need license or) Tj T* 0 Tw (registration or brochure duty attaches to them as such.) Tj T* ET
