BT 1 0 0 1 0 315.804 Tm 1.465846 Tw 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: The unlicensed online pension-plan offer is unlawful on both the licensing and advertising) Tj T* 0 Tw .600857 Tw (gates, so the Insurance Commission may issue a cease-and-desist order against it and the sellers) Tj T* 0 Tw (face fines and criminal exposure.) Tj  T* .0045 Tw (Under Sec. 10 of RA 9829, no person may operate as a pre-need company without a Commission) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.268571 Tw (license. Under Sec. 14, every plan intended for public sale needs a registration statement filed) Tj T* 0 Tw .124286 Tw (within forty-five days of licensing. Under Sec. 18, no pre-need advertising may run without prior) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.807 Tw (Commission approval. Under Primamanila Plans v. SEC \(G.R. No. 193791, 2014\), a website) Tj T* 0 Tw 4.115 Tw (offer of pension plans with bank-deposit payment instructions and no license sustains a) Tj T* 0 Tw 4.037 Tw (cease-and-desist order. Under Secs. 53\(c\) and 54, unauthorized selling draws fines on a) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.129818 Tw (thirty-percent and forty-percent and license-loss ladder plus one year of imprisonment and) Tj T* 0 Tw (triple-price fines.) Tj  T* 1.56 Tw (Here, the company holds no license yet offers pension plans to the public online and collects) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.448 Tw (through bank deposits. The missing license breaches Sec. 10 and the missing registration) Tj T* 0 Tw .519692 Tw (breaches Sec. 14 while the unapproved website solicitation breaches Sec. 18. That the payments) Tj T* 0 Tw .082154 Tw (look like ordinary bank deposits changes nothing because plan consideration paid through a bank) Tj T* 0 Tw (remains plan consideration. The Primamanila pattern is matched element for element.) Tj  T* 1.494462 Tw (The Commission may therefore shut the offer down by cease-and-desist order, and the sellers) Tj T* 0 Tw (answer for administrative fines and criminal liability for unregistered selling.) Tj T* ET
