BT 1 0 0 1 0 297.804 Tm 1.4712 Tw 18 TL /F2 12 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: The provider owes no memorial services on these facts, so the dismissal of the planholder ) Tj T* 0 Tw (claim stands and the family bears the outside funeral and replacement-casket costs alone.) Tj ( ) Tj T* 2.13 Tw (Under RA 9829 and the plan-is-law rule of Gaw v. CA \(G.R. No. 147748, 2006\), the clear ) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.109538 Tw (stipulations of the pre-need plan control literally between the parties. Under Gaw, the provider ) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.4056 Tw (holding the sole and exclusive right to arrange services with a mortuary of its choice requires ) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.872 Tw (notice directly to and acknowledged by the provider before the family acts, with time of the ) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.650857 Tw (essence. Under Sec. 3, doubts favor the planholder, but liberality never rewrites a clear term. ) Tj T* 0 Tw .360857 Tw (Under Dio v. St. Ferdinand Memorial Park \(G.R. No. 169578, 2006\), an adhesion contract binds ) Tj T* 0 Tw (as written because the adherer was free to reject it entirely.) Tj ( ) Tj T* .246 Tw (Here, the family engaged an outside funeral home at once upon the death of the mother and let it ) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.504571 Tw (embalm the body and supply a casket before notifying the provider only that evening. The ) Tj T* 0 Tw 4.038545 Tw (evening notice after embalming and casketing preempted the sole arrangement right and ) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.404 Tw (breached the imperative acknowledged-notice term. The later substitution of a different casket ) Tj T* 0 Tw .368308 Tw (breached the pre-selected-casket term whose upgrade cost Gaw assigns to the family alone. That ) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.007385 Tw (the plan is an adhesion contract avails nothing because Dio enforces clear adhesion terms ) Tj T* 0 Tw (literally.) Tj ( ) Tj T* .417231 Tw (The provider therefore properly refused the memorial services, and the dismissal stands with the) Tj T* 0 Tw ET
